<title>USA: Vacation Break in stock deal to buy Berkley.</title>
<headline>Vacation Break in stock deal to buy Berkley.</headline>
<dateline>FORT LAUDERDALE, FLA. 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vacation Break USA said it agreed to buy The Berkley Group, a privately held developer and marketer of timeshare resort properties in Florida and Virginia, in a stock transaction.</p>
<p>Under terms of the transaction, Vacation Break will issue 21 million shares of its common stock to Berkley Group shareholders, Vacation Break said.</p>
<p>Following the transaction, Berkley Group chairman and chief executive Jim Lambert will become co-chairman and chief executive of the Vacation Break USA.</p>
<p>Vacation Break officials were not immediately available to comment.</p>
</text>
